// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P926656652" "The Sword that was Forgotten"
// DetailString :
"P3008061077" "Ward, the overspell of the Midnight Mansion's defensive glyphs in Night Ward, had a simple request; return the other errant spells to him so they could all be family again. You went searching for the errant Animus Arcana, spells who, through a complicated series of events involving the manifestation of the bizarre realm of Night Ward in the first place and Percy Winkley's death to boot, had gained sentience and life. You found a group of them following a charismatic and wise spell named Clarity, but as it turned out, you weren't the only one looking for them. The Talons of Vengeance had found their way into Night Ward as well and were intent on turning even these sentient magical spells to their cause."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3440621750" "Ward, the overspell of the Midnight Mansion's defensive glyphs in Night Ward, had a simple request; return the other errant spells to him so they could all be family again. You went searching for the errant Animus Arcana, spells who, through a complicated series of events involving the manifestation of the bizarre realm of Night Ward in the first place and Percy Winkley's death to boot, had gained sentience and life. You found a group of them following a charismatic and wise spell named Clarity, but as it turned out, you weren't the only one looking for them. The Talons of Vengeance had found their way into Night Ward as well and were intent on turning even these sentient magical spells to their cause.<br><br>Clarity didn't want to return to Ward, wishing instead to be, for the first time, independent, and many of the Animus Arcana shared her view. Ward, ever fatherly, wanted to do right by his children and so sent you instead to make sure the Talons didn't corrupt more of them. You hunted down a group of Talons doing just that and learned that soon the Coven would be returned to life and then the magic that feels would join them and exact vengeance upon the world and their mistress would be freed from the Eternal Prison."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2056966863" "Ward, the overspell of the Midnight Mansion's defensive glyphs in Night Ward, had a simple request; return the other errant spells to him so they could all be family again. You went searching for the errant Animus Arcana, spells who, through a complicated series of events involving the manifestation of the bizarre realm of Night Ward in the first place and Percy Winkley's death to boot, had gained sentience and life. You found a group of them following a charismatic and wise spell named Clarity, but as it turned out, you weren't the only one looking for them. The Talons of Vengeance had found their way into Night Ward as well and were intent on turning even these sentient magical spells to their cause.<br><br>Clarity didn't want to return to Ward, wishing instead to be, for the first time, independent, and many of the Animus Arcana shared her view. Ward, ever fatherly, wanted to do right by his children and so sent you instead to make sure the Talons didn't corrupt more of them. You hunted down a group of Talons doing just that and learned that soon the Coven would be returned to life and then the magic that feels would join them and exact vengeance upon the world and their mistress would be freed from the Eternal Prison.<br><br>This news meant little to Ward other than concern, but after speaking with Montague and referencing Tremaine's Book of the Dead you discovered that the Eternal Prison was a place where evil souls were kept from the rest of reality. Together, with Nadia, you investigated the final resting place of her and Serene's old coven to see if that is what the Talons were referring to. To your horror you witnessed the Talons using Animus Arcana and captured Seers to resurrect Nadia's sisters. You then learned that their plan was to free Sorceress Serene from the Eternal Prison, but first they would need to consume the Midnighters now that Master Midnight's armor was lost to them."

